{"lines": ["Next, India. Roopkund, a small lake high in the Himalayas, at about five thousand metres. When the snow melts, human skeletons are visible at its edge.", "A forest ranger, Hari Kishan Madhwal, rediscovered them in 1942. At first, British authorities feared they were casualties of a hidden Japanese invasion force. But the bones were far too old.", "Remains of more than three hundred people have been found.", "A local legend says a king, Raja Jasdhaval, his pregnant queen and a dance troupe were on a pilgrimage to the goddess Nanda Devi, when a storm of huge hailstones killed them all.", "In the 1950s, the Anthropological Survey of India found head injuries from round objects falling from above. Oxford dated the deaths to about 850 CE. It fit the legend perfectly.", "Then came the DNA. Researchers studied thirty-eight individuals, with both radiocarbon dating and genome-wide analysis.", "Twenty-three had South Asian ancestry, dated about 800 CE. Fourteen had ancestry typical of the eastern Mediterranean, dated about 1800 CE. One had Southeast Asian ancestry, also about 1800.", "Two separate events, a thousand years apart. Not one catastrophe.", "Rule four. Check the date, and the DNA, before you trust a perfect story."], "words": [["Next,", 0.0, 0.2], ["India.", 0.2, 0.7], ["Roopkund,", 0.7, 1.7], ["a", 1.7, 1.76], ["small", 1.76, 1.98], ["lake", 1.98, 2.28], ["high", 2.28, 2.54], ["in", 2.54, 2.74], ["the", 2.74, 2.82], ["Himalayas,", 2.82, 3.5], ["at", 3.64, 3.82], ["about", 3.82, 4.02], ["five", 4.02, 4.607], ["thousand", 4.607, 5.193], ["metres.", 5.193, 5.78], ["When", 5.78, 6.0], ["the", 6.0, 6.1], ["snow", 6.1, 6.3], ["melts,", 6.3, 6.6], ["human", 6.6, 6.98], ["skeletons", 6.98, 7.36], ["are", 7.36, 7.78], ["visible", 7.78, 7.94], ["at", 7.94, 8.32], ["its", 8.32, 8.48], ["edge.", 8.48, 8.74], ["A", 9.64, 9.72], ["forest", 9.72, 9.94], ["ranger,", 9.94, 10.5], ["Hari", 10.5, 11.067], ["Kishan", 11.067, 11.633], ["Madhwal,", 11.633, 12.2], ["redisco